cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use or adapt the SAN TOMMASO prompt, please cite this release; use the Zenodo version-specific DOI once available.
title: 'SAN TOMMASO: A Single Integrated Prompt for Source-Traceable Scientific Manuscript Auditing'
version: '0.6'
type: software
license: CC-BY-4.0
authors:
- family-names: Taffache
  given-names: Paolo
  affiliation: General and Pediatric Anesthesia and Intensive Care Unit, IRCCS Azienda Ospedaliero-Universitaria di Bologna
abstract: Unvalidated, freely reusable single master prompt designed to coordinate source-traceable draft audits of scientific
  manuscripts across 17 proposed domains, with explicit access limitations, evidence-ledger records, staged output and human
  adjudication. No empirical performance or effectiveness claim is made.
keywords:
- research integrity
- manuscript auditing
- large language models
- source verification
- human-in-the-loop
- experimental prompt
- reproducibility
